# Academic & Professional Website

A lightweight, responsive, and Markdown-driven portfolio website designed for deployment on GitHub Pages. Built with zero-dependency native web technologies, client-side Markdown rendering, and an industrial color palette.

---

## 🎨 Color Scheme Palette

The design utilizes a cohesive five-color palette built on standard CSS custom properties:

| Color Name | Hex Code | Description & Usage |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Charcoal** | `#565264` | Deep, smoky industrial tone used for main headers, footers, and code blocks. |
| **Dim Grey** | `#706677` | Grounded, resilient grey used for primary brand elements and subheadings. |
| **Dusty Mauve** | `#a6808c` | Dusky mauve-grey accent used for link highlights, active states, and borders. |
| **Almond Silk** | `#ccb7ae` | Gentle beige-pink used for navigation link defaults and secondary accents. |
| **Dust Grey** | `#d6cfcb` | Soft, stone-toned grey used for the primary website background. |

---

## 📁 Repository Structure

```text
my-website/
├── .nojekyll           # Disables Jekyll processing on GitHub Pages
├── index.html          # Main HTML entry point and navigation shell
├── README.md           # Project documentation
├── css/
│   ├── variables.css   # Color palette tokens and global CSS variables
│   ├── style.css       # Core layout, header, and footer styles
│   └── components.css  # Card components, buttons, and Markdown typography
├── js/
│   └── main.js         # Client-side hash router and Markdown fetcher
└── content/            # Core site content written in Markdown
    ├── teaching.md     # Teaching philosophy, courses, and mentorship
    ├── research.md     # Research themes, publications, and grants
    ├── outreach.md     # Public engagement, service, and media
    └── projects.md     # Open-source tools, applications, and frameworks
